	(text "Sensor inputs: notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 134.62 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "a7df40b2-098c-57f8-b959-318341f6629c")
	)
	(text "For 3-wire PNP (sourcing) 24 V sensors, e.g. Autonics PRD08 / PR series (brown +V, black OUT, blue 0 V).\nNPN (sinking) sensors need a different input circuit.\n\nSame circuit as the MES4-Flasher sensor channels 3 / 4 (PB6 / PC15), without the INA226 supply monitors.\nGPIO budget: all 14 module pins are used (Main sheet, MES4-CIF §2c). More sensors need inputs on\nI²C1, e.g. a TCA9535 expander (0x20-0x27), polled.\n\nPB6: the ST bootloader enables a 25-55 kΩ pull-up on PB6 (blank chip only); with the 10k pull-down it\nreads LOW, which is harmless for an input. PC15: input only (RTC-domain pin, CIF rule 10): fine here.\nInterrupts: PB6 → EXTI6. PC15 shares EXTI15 with PA15 (INA226 ALERT): give EXTI15 to PC15 (sensor 2)\nand poll ALERT, which the INA226 latches (MASK/ENABLE LEN = 1), so no fault is missed.\nNo back-powering: the PC817 collectors run from +3V3_MOD (module finger 4), so nothing drives the\nmodule pins while it is unpowered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "cfe50895-e0f1-573b-b6dc-c9568442a967")
	)
